WEBVTT

00:00:00.003 --> 00:00:05.876
Open AURA and select Check microphone and
sound. The application uses your system

00:00:05.876 --> 00:00:11.822
audio devices. Allow microphone access in
the browser, then check the input level.

00:00:11.822 --> 00:00:18.058
This tutorial uses a synthetic microphone
signal and transcript; it cannot verify your

00:00:18.058 --> 00:00:20.378
physical microphone or speakers.

00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:26.726
Select Record, speak a short request, then
finish recording. The recognized words

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:32.616
appear as an editable draft. Review names,
numbers and technical terms before sending.

00:00:32.616 --> 00:00:38.232
If no words appear, check operating system
microphone permissions and the selected

00:00:38.232 --> 00:00:40.629
system input before starting again.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:47.151
Send the reviewed message and read the
answer. AURA can discuss your context, but a

00:00:47.151 --> 00:00:52.941
conversation cannot authorize a maintenance
operation. For hands-free turns, start a

00:00:52.941 --> 00:00:58.455
conversation explicitly and stop it when
finished. Page changes, hidden tabs and

00:00:58.455 --> 00:01:01.005
Escape interrupt capture or playback.

00:01:01.806 --> 00:01:07.827
Use conversation history to reopen saved
exchanges. Attach only the documents needed

00:01:07.827 --> 00:01:13.634
for the question and check their extraction.
Text remains available when audio is

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:18.723
unavailable. This guide demonstrates
interface behavior with controlled

00:01:18.723 --> 00:01:23.956
responses, not model accuracy or successful
audio capture on your device.
